# owed-derivations-c (unit b7, receipt-bl706.sh) starts of reconcile/apply.sh and the helper beside it (BL-879 grammar). Every other
# drive is in process: the receipt loads apply.sh once (inproc_load) and calls apl_main through inproc_run, and calls the helper's
# dd_main through inproc_run with nothing loaded, so each is one pass under its own inproc: row. The two cli cells are cell eq's CLI
# halves, the apply.sh outcomes that differ (a refusal, exit 2 naming the option, and a passing pull): each is started once as
# FXCELL=cli-<id> bash "$APPLY" and compared byte for byte (stdout, stderr, exit) with the in-process answer on the same input.
# Every other apply.sh drive reaches the differential, which apply.sh starts as a child that needs a start of apply.sh as its logged
# parent: e2e-apply-<n>, numbered in the order the receipt runs them. The helper's starts are those children, nested below.
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-1 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-2 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-3 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-4 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-5 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-6 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-7 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-8 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-9 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
e2e core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh e2e-apply-10 why=apply.sh starts the differential helper as a child whose start is covered only under a start of apply.sh as its logged parent
cli core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh cli-pass
cli core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh cli-refuse
nested core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/apply.sh core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/derivation-differential.sh why=apply.sh hands the pull to the differential helper with bash "$DD_HELPER" (record mode, its own temp dir, EXIT trap and exit status read back by apply.sh); an in-process apply starts that child exactly as a CLI apply does
